  minutes after we were supposed to close  he made us basically keep the store open  and some reason everyone else complied  with him to be honest I think everyone  was a little bit scared of him the thing  with Rob was he would usually grab  receipts from either  or people's trays or the trash fill out  like the little survey on the receipts  and give it to us for free food  one day we caught him on camera doing  that he told him no that could all be  kind of forgivable because he seemed to  be a bit down on his luck but he would  actually come in and on his laptop we  actually caught him watching porn near  the play area multiple times and then  once we told him no he would just go in  the bathroom for a while and then come  back other than watching porn yet the  play area he would always be cussing on  the phone cussing at his laptop cussing  at us because the Wi-Fi was slow we kept  telling the managers like we need him  out he's a terrible customer he's barely  a customer he's creating a really harsh  work environment for us and the  customers it all came to a head one day  when he was cussing you're at a family  with little kids so the table were like  nah you're out you're out of here my  favorite part about having him gone was  the time he tried to sneak back in the  drive-thru line we took his order we ran  back out to see if that was really him  we let him wait about 20 minutes in the  lines it was rush hour and then when he  got to the window were like we're sorry  you're Ben he was extremely mad and he  cussed all the way out of the drive-thru  and yeah that was a story of Rob I hope  I never run into him again we all hope  that because he was honestly a really  big jerk one time there was this guy he  was a little on the larger aside which  is perfectly fine  every Tuesday it was twenty nine cent he  was either hamburgers or cheeseburgers  but 29 cent burgers this rather large  man came in and we asked what would you  like and he ordered the burgers and we  said how many would you like  and he said all of them well there was  this like hot I wasn't sure how to react  when somebody said all of them basically  what he wanted to order was every single  burger that we had in the restaurant  called the manager and I was like what  is what do i do how do we you ring up  every burger in the restaurant I think  we topped it off at about a hundred and  so we literally just rang them up gave  it to him in multiple bags to this day  we're about 90% sure he ate all of them  in the parking lot  it was it was on Sunday late afternoon  early evening I remember being at the  register Sunday's was typically when  they put all that schedule for the  workweek but I remember my coworker  coming in that day walking into the back  and all I heard was just what dog just  being upset at their schedule and it  hours being cut she got really all you  hear in the background was why would you  do that what the business like what  would you cut my hours let this person  just starts like flipping burgers over  maybe flippin fries over everybody in  the front we just kept all looking at  each other like is this really happening  llama cows is the greatest place in the  history of the universe there's always  gonna be some horror stories I was one  of the craziest nights at the time  that's my heart and crazy story and  having a crazy co-worker my experience  was actually decent at least for a first  job and especially for a first job at a  fast food place I do have some horror  stories  [Music]

